<header><p class="st-kicker">other · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Irish Free State</h1><p class="st-meta">1922 CE – 1937 CE · capital Dublin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The self-governing dominion of twenty-six Irish counties established by the Anglo-Irish Treaty in 1922, the forerunner of modern Ireland.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-irish-treaty">Anglo-Irish Treaty</a> of December 1921 created the Irish Free State as a dominion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/commonwealth-of-nations">British Commonwealth</a>, with the British monarch as head of state and an oath of fidelity. It came into being on 6 December 1922, during the civil war between pro-Treaty and anti-Treaty republicans.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Free State's first government under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/w-t-cosgrave">W. T. Cosgrave</a> won the civil war in 1923, built a civil service, an unarmed police force, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garda-siochana">Garda Siochana</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-shannon">Shannon</a> hydroelectric scheme. It joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> in 1923. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eamon-de-valera">Eamon de Valera's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fianna-fail">Fianna Fail</a> took power in 1932 and dismantled Treaty links, removing the oath and fighting an economic war with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>A new constitution, approved by referendum in 1937, replaced the Free State with Ireland, or Eire.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/irish-free-state.jpg" alt="Irish Free State" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Éire · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ireland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1922 CE – 1937 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dublin</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>W. T. Cosgrave, Eamon de Valera, Kevin O'Higgins</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Saorstat Eireann</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1930&amp;focus=irish-free-state" aria-label="Irish Free State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4541 343 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Irish Free State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4861 599L4861 599M4861 599L4861 599M4861 599L4997 651M4861 599L4997 651M4861 599L4861 599"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4861 599h0M4861 599h0M4997 651h0M4997 651h0M4861 599h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4861 599h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4861 599h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dublin. <a href="/atlas?year=1930&amp;focus=irish-free-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
